{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156936-tyon-pijavica-are-unplayable","id":1156936,"title":"[TYoN] Pijavica are unplayable?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-08T02:35:48-08:00","id":1156936,"title":"[TYoN] Pijavica are unplayable?","content":"I wanted to add Slavic vampires to my games, being Slav myself. I remembered then <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Tzimisce\" target=\"_blank\">Tzimisce</a> Clan from VtM that made Voivodate state, created flesh and blood experiments ( like <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Vozhd\" target=\"_blank\">Vozhd</a> ) and made many other interesting ideas. Pijavica seems to work at least in flesh changing aspect to it. Until we look in to <b>Thousand Years of Night </b>and read they are some kind mutated \u2018blobs of Blood\u2019 until Blood Potency 4 and from Blood Potency 8. I thought they will be like maybe on BP 0 or BP 1 at max this Blood thing, not <b>almost 1/3 of their unlife</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It makes running characters like Dracula from Bram Stoker almost impossible till 3 centuries in to unlife of Pijavica. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or do I read it wrongly somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T02:39:22-08:00","id":1156937,"title":"","content":"It only takes 150 years to get to blood potency 4, not 300.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T02:43:44-08:00","id":1156939,"title":"","content":"I haven't got TYoN but all the other clan banes don't kick in until you drop a humanity, I know this isn't great but it's something you could use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T02:58:33-08:00","id":1156941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156936-tyon-pijavica-are-unplayable?p=1156939#post1156939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't got TYoN but all the other clan banes don't kick in until you drop a humanity, I know this isn't great but it's something you could use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pijavica Clan Bane is also based on Blood Potency - I could understand it was somehow related to Humanity - like rest of Clan Banes - , but I think devs wanted to show how inhuman they are. Well, they made them so inhuman, that running them in human population is almost impossible. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-08-2017, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T03:26:55-08:00","id":1156945,"title":"","content":"They went extinct for a reason, Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T04:04:07-08:00","id":1156956,"title":"","content":"They're in an elders book with alternate chargen rules for starting at blood potency 5. <br /> <br /> They're entirely playable, as long as you start at blood potency 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T04:22:24-08:00","id":1156960,"title":"","content":"\u200bWell, I want to use them as 'nearly extinct Slavic vamps', not some blood ooze, over and over again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156936-tyon-pijavica-are-unplayable?p=1156956#post1156956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're in an elders book with alternate chargen rules for starting at blood potency 5.<br /> <br /> They're entirely playable, as long as you start at blood potency 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Okay, so I got rules good that they need high Blood Potency to human-like. If that's the case, I may do alternative Clan Bane for them in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1152460-2e-hack-%E2%80%93-alternative-clan-banes\">my Clan Banes Hack topic</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T06:57:26-08:00","id":1156985,"title":"","content":"They're playable at anything except blood potency 1. If you really want to play one, find a way to start at BP 3 and you'll be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T10:30:08-08:00","id":1157049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156936-tyon-pijavica-are-unplayable?p=1156985#post1156985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're playable at anything except blood potency 1. If you really want to play one, find a way to start at BP 3 and you'll be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I look as ST here - I do not run <b>Vampire</b> for players, I run it as NPCs. Even if I like general idea of Clan 'coming from the Blood, literally', making vampire to hangs on and wait 100 years to become somehow human-like is simply... too long, I guess? I think I can 'wait' for those few days, maybe weeks. But come on - <b>Who would created Pijavica neonate so he need next 100 years wait till he could DO something in human society?</b> ( Yes, it's rhetorical question, cause I know I would not. )<br /> <br /> Their Bane is just too stagnated - it changes once per 25/50 years, where most other Clan Banes are related to Humanity levels in direct manner - so they <b><i>change with the rhythm of the story in chronicle</i></b>, not just years clock of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-08-2017, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T11:06:31-08:00","id":1157059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156936-tyon-pijavica-are-unplayable?p=1157049#post1157049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their Bane is just too stagnated - it changes once per 25/50 years, where most other Clan Banes are related to Humanity levels in direct manner - so they <b><i>change with the rhythm of the story in chronicle</i></b>, not just years clock of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Diablerie and the creation of progeny are still things they can do, I'll note, as is spending Experiences on Blood Potency. The only clan Discipline they'll have any trouble with is Animalism and the nearest thing to a hard lockout on their ability to act in early nights is the corebook's mentioned forty-night larval stage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T13:08:32-08:00","id":1157104,"title":"","content":"My solution would be to create a Cruac (or other ritual magic) ritual at whatever level (probably 4+?) that allows a Pijavica to possess a dead body for X time. It doesn't rot, so long as they spend a point of blood per night, etc etc. Would bind the kiddos pretty well to their sires (if indeed the sire is the one who performs the ritual for them) and would probably make whatever form of magic they're using very very important to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T15:10:51-08:00","id":1157135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156936-tyon-pijavica-are-unplayable?p=1157059#post1157059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diablerie and the creation of progeny are still things they can do, I'll note, as is spending Experiences on Blood Potency. The only clan Discipline they'll have any trouble with is Animalism and the nearest thing to a hard lockout on their ability to act in early nights is the corebook's mentioned forty-night larval stage.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156936-tyon-pijavica-are-unplayable?p=1157104#post1157104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My solution would be to create a Cruac (or other ritual magic) ritual at whatever level (probably 4+?) that allows a Pijavica to possess a dead body for X time. It doesn't rot, so long as they spend a point of blood per night, etc etc. Would bind the kiddos pretty well to their sires (if indeed the sire is the one who performs the ritual for them) and would probably make whatever form of magic they're using very very important to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are just in-game fixes for bad mechanics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I really wanted to make Pijavica main 'Slavic Clan', with Ventrue and Mekhet as 'imperialists coming to East Europe' in times of Rome. Clan to be playable <b>should not</b> need of Diablerie or Cruac Rituals ( which will not exist till those 1800's with Circle of Crone ) just to make vampires to work with human society in some way - even Nosferatu have easier times to work with humanity, for God sake!<br /> <br /> I'm okay with idea of forty-night larval stage - I would probably short it to few nights, but's it's more 'a story dynamic' reasons than anything - but from that period neonate should more or less be able to come in relations with humanity. Other way around, we have Pijavica <i>only</i> as Clan to make animalistic undead antagonists, nothing more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And we <i>have</i> inhuman Gangrels for that, too, don't we?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T15:38:05-08:00","id":1157141,"title":"","content":"Pijavica weren't written as the 'Slavic Clan' primarily though. They were written as the 'blood monsters that erupt from bloated corpses Clan'. Surely you can use something besides the Pijavica? Think of how the indigenous Mexican and Spanish vampires are portrayed in <i>Shadows of Mexico</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 11-08-2017, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T15:45:11-08:00","id":1157143,"title":"","content":"These guys are mentioned in the VtR2e corebook, right? I remember reading about them and thinking how cool and Mythos-like they were. Not every Kindred lineage should be human to begin with, as the Kindred themselves don\u2019t have a common origin. And the idea they\u2019re a twisted echo of Prometheans merely adds to their creepy coolness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T15:56:28-08:00","id":1157144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156936-tyon-pijavica-are-unplayable?p=1157135#post1157135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clan to be playable <b>should not</b> need of Diablerie or Cruac Rituals ( which will not exist till those 1800's with Circle of Crone ) just to make vampires to work with human society in some way - even Nosferatu have easier times to work with humanity, for God sake!</div> </div> </div> </div>As Thorbes points out, they were a weird phenomenon with limits that kept them from becoming more prolific. As-written they're explicitly running on a deficit that proper Kindred are stable enough to avoid without rapidly boosting their Blood Potency and/or rolling Humanity very frequently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm okay with idea of forty-night larval stage - I would probably short it to few nights, but's it's more 'a story dynamic' reasons than anything - but from that period neonate should more or less be able to come in relations with humanity. </div> </div> </div>The whole deal with the Pijavica is that they didn't have the starting flexibility to keep their numbers up. Converting them to a more typical clan without softening the impact of their condition is best suited by enabling them to raise their Blood Potency quickly through systems of diablerie and Blood Beats, by giving their sires a method like Jiang Shi have to create their progeny with higher starting Blood Potency, or by using weird experimental Devotions like the one Vlastislav developed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other way around, we have Pijavica <i>only</i> as Clan to make animalistic undead antagonists, nothing more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And we <i>have</i> inhuman Gangrels for that, too, don't we? </div> </div> </div>The Pijavica are distinguished from the Gangrel by their being alien on top of atavistic; the Savages' bane instead doubles down on feral behavior. The Gangrel are not vampiric versions of The Thing and do not present the same challenges to play. If you just want a clan of Slavic origins, there are less awkward options at your disposal than trying to make the Pijavica into a normal clan rather than one with such a close tie to the alienating aspects of vampirism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T16:05:15-08:00","id":1157145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156936-tyon-pijavica-are-unplayable?p=1157144#post1157144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you just want a clan of Slavic origins, there are less awkward options at your disposal than trying to make the Pijavica into a normal clan rather than one with such a close tie to the alienating aspects of vampirism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, let's hear it. Because classical Slavic vampires from myths returns from their grave after being sucked by other vampires, just like typical Revenant in 2E. In Slavic mythos, I did not found anything truly interesting for the Clan creation - like Tzimisce flesh changing or Pijavica alien mindset from start.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156936-tyon-pijavica-are-unplayable?p=1157144#post1157144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole deal with the Pijavica is that they didn't have the starting flexibility to keep their numbers up. Converting them to a more typical clan without softening the impact of their condition is best suited by enabling them to raise their Blood Potency quickly through systems of diablerie and Blood Beats, by giving their sires a method like Jiang Shi have to create their progeny with higher starting Blood Potency, or by using weird experimental Devotions like the one Vlastislav developed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Diablerie I pass, as I do not start as most heinious vampires act as opening solution for whole Clan. But I'm more interested in listening about Jiang Shi or Vlastislav solutions.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T17:09:26-08:00","id":1157156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156936-tyon-pijavica-are-unplayable?p=1157145#post1157145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, let's hear it. Because classical Slavic vampires from myths returns from their grave after being sucked by other vampires, just like typical Revenant in 2E. In Slavic mythos, I did not found anything truly interesting for the Clan creation - like Tzimisce flesh changing or Pijavica alien mindset from start.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you just want the Tzimisce, you'd have better luck looking at conversions of the Tzimisce like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\">Yossarian's</a> made as part of regular Masquiem fan-material.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Diablerie I pass, as I do not start as most heinious vampires act as opening solution for whole Clan. But I'm more interested in listening about Jiang Shi or Vlastislav solutions. </div> </div> </div>The Jiang Shi can take the heart of the &quot;extraordinarily pure&quot; person whose blood they need to replace an ordinary person's with to make them into a Jiang Shi; taking the heart means the progeny starts with Blood Potency 2 instead of 1.<br /> <br /> Vlastislav's got a Dominate 5/Protean 3 Devotion that can turn a willing Kindred with Blood Potency less than his own into another Pijavica after a couple of days, though the presented narrative state suggests this is an unreliable process that's liable to stir up some conflict due to a need for older and stronger vampires than fresh Embraces can provide.<br /> <br /> You might simply apply a variant rule like the Phantoms' effective possession of multiple banes and ability to return to their &quot;graves&quot; and just give the Pijavica a dot of Blood Potency every time they lose a dot of Humanity, particularly if you're only running these characters as NPCs in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-08-2017, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T17:17:01-08:00","id":1157157,"title":"","content":"There's also the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Norvegi\" target=\"_blank\">Norvegi</a>, who originated in Scandinavia after the Grettir.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't place too much credit in diablerie being considered the 'most heinous' of vampire acts, it's fairly common and the Tradition is supposed to have popped up just to staunch an outbreak of a diablerie-induced plague. It's likely held up by elders to keep neonates from getting ideas about using them as shortcuts to power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T00:01:34-08:00","id":1157207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156936-tyon-pijavica-are-unplayable?p=1157156#post1157156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you just want the Tzimisce, you'd have better luck looking at conversions of the Tzimisce like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\">Yossarian's</a> made as part of regular Masquiem fan-material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not need the Tzimisce per se - rather some cool Slavic Clan. Tzimsce can pop up as some Bloodline or something. I <i>really </i>like Pijavica as concept - I just do not agree with too restrictive mechanics of it shown in <b>Thousand Years of Night</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156936-tyon-pijavica-are-unplayable?p=1157156#post1157156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might simply apply a variant rule like the Phantoms' effective possession of multiple banes and ability to return to their &quot;graves&quot; and just give the Pijavica a dot of Blood Potency every time they lose a dot of Humanity, particularly if you're only running these characters as NPCs in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>By Phantoms you mean here Hollow Mekhets? Or what group?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156936-tyon-pijavica-are-unplayable?p=1157156#post1157156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Jiang Shi can take the heart of the &quot;extraordinarily pure&quot; person whose blood they need to replace an ordinary person's with to make them into a Jiang Shi; taking the heart means the progeny starts with Blood Potency 2 instead of 1.<br /> <br /> Vlastislav's got a Dominate 5/Protean 3 Devotion that can turn a willing Kindred with Blood Potency less than his own into another Pijavica after a couple of days, though the presented narrative state suggests this is an unreliable process that's liable to stir up some conflict due to a need for older and stronger vampires than fresh Embraces can provide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting ideas, good to know those.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T00:26:30-08:00","id":1157212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1156936-tyon-pijavica-are-unplayable?p=1157207#post1157207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By Phantoms you mean here Hollow Mekhets? Or what group?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the Jiang Shi, i.e. the clan of vampires nicknamed the Phantoms in their writeup in the VtR2e core rulebook which describes all the ways in which they differ from normal Kindred and consequently have typically lower numbers. Check page 255.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T06:06:17-08:00","id":1157258,"title":"","content":"Eh you have Betrayed or whatever they were called from VII book. They are slavic and hate other vamps. Or you can bump bloodline like Yagnatia or Tismanu(orthodox monks from ordo dracul) to full clan status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}